WEBVTT

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:32.426
but she was likable,
intelligent and talkative.

00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.586
And yet just a short while later,

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:37.436
her interviewer told me
that she had totally failed,

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:40.446
that she couldn't string
two words together.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:42.100
The screening philosophy

00:01:42.124 --> 00:01:46.776
of "let's pick our employees
by viewing them at their worst,"

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.126
not only overlooks disabled people

00:01:49.150 --> 00:01:52.646
but anyone whose shine
is diminished under harsh pressure.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:55.326
We developed the reverse screening process

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:56.573
to find potential.

00:01:56.597 --> 00:01:58.116
And as the name implies,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.296
we go about things
practically the opposite way